{
  "name": "UberLLM: product photo → studio spin video",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Product photo → studio spin video (UberLLM)\nA clean turntable-style clip for a store page or an ad, from one photo:\n1. **Make studio still**: `google/nano-banana-2-edit` puts the product alone on a clean studio background (1:1).\n2. **Start video**: `kling/kling-o3-standard-image-to-video` turns it slowly, camera still, 5 s.\n3. **Spin video** holds the clip as binary `data`.\n\nThe clip takes the shape of the still: set `aspect_ratio` to `1:1`, `4:5` or `9:16`. The model draws the sides it cannot see in your photo, so check the result against the real product. A turn shows best on a product with a label or an uneven shape.\n\n### Setup (2 minutes)\n1. Get a key at https://uberllm.dev (sign in with your email, add credit).\n2. Open any **UberLLM** HTTP node → Credential → **Create new** → *Header Auth*:\n   - Name: `Authorization`\n   - Value: `Bearer YOUR_UBERLLM_KEY`\n   Every UberLLM node in this workflow uses this one credential.\n3. Edit the **Settings** node, then click **Execute workflow**.\n\n`product_image_url` must be a public `https://` link to the product photo.\n\n### Price\nListed on 2026-11-19: 1 still at $0.04 each + a 5 s clip at $0.07 per second = about $0.39. Live prices: https://uberllm.dev/ai-ad-creative-api\n\n### What you pay\n- The start reply shows the price now (`estimated_cost_usd`). The bill is what the provider charged, which can differ if the job moves to another provider.\n- Your ceiling is `max_cost` in **Settings**: a job that would cost more is refused or cancelled at no charge.\n- A video that fails or runs out of time costs nothing: the whole hold comes back.\n- Credit you buy does not expire while your account is open.\n- No UberLLM fee on requests. Adding credit by card costs 5.5% + $0.50.\n\n### Files are short-lived\nPicture links are kept about 15 minutes and video links about 3 hours, and they need your key. The workflow downloads every result at once, so the last node holds the files as binary data: send them to Drive, S3 or your ad tool from there.\n\n### Why the still is uploaded\nA result link needs your key, so a video model cannot open it. **Upload still** puts the picture in your UberLLM files (kept 24 hours) and the clip starts from that upload.\n",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 600
      },
      "id": "23263db1-89cd-54b1-9918-7fec5ba0a9a6",
      "name": "About",
